primaryOutcomes.description:
AE occurring throughout the study period will be evaluated using the CTCAE V5.0 standard.

AE/SAE were evaluated by laboratory examination and imageological examination, measuring method：

1. Head MRI, whole spine MRI, chest CT examination;
2. Changes in vital signs, 12-lead electrocardiogram, ultrasound (thyroid, abdomen, heart, genitourinary system) examination, and neurological signs;
3. Changes in blood routine, urine routine, stool routine, finger end blood oxygen saturation, serum immunoglobulin, cerebrospinal fluid routine, liver function, kidney function, electrolyte, muscle enzyme, lipid, blood glucose, glycated hemoglobin, coagulation function, tumor markers, various hepatitis viruses, treponema lutei antibodies, HIV antibodies and other indicators.

